A||N||2||grinthock||Plenum Cleaning?  Methods?||||5||
Z||000000||grinthock||04-21-2001||09:38 AM||||Hi everyone, was looking at my salt stained, oxidyed plenum and was thinking, how thick is the metal on it?  I have a 87 with the Engraved "FIERO" on it, I was thinking, all the area that are NOT RED could I take the light sanding disc on my Dremel and just detail sand the metal areas?<P>What has everyone else done to clean it?<P>also what's the head called that you use to remove the plenum?||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||04-21-2001||07:16 PM||||DON'T SAND! You'll get nasty results. You can use a cotton polshing wheel on your Dremel with some metal polish. That'll do fine. If it's so bad you want to take it off, get it media blasted and have it powdercoated. Cost a bit more then a can of engine paint, but you can't argue with the results! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712481&Sequence=5"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-22-2001||01:34 PM||||And if you do decide to get it powdercoated it wouldn't be a bad idea to sand down the casting flash on the plenum. Its a small detail but it really looks nice!||||reg||14
